  "guide": {
    "corridor": [
      {
        "body": "Your first life is over. Your soul waits here, between lives.\n\n- When you close this guide, the world shows you *the life you lived*. Its button leads on.\n- Make your *Last Wish*. It decides which Unique Skills can be yours.\n- Then begin your *reincarnation*, or face your *Trial of the Soul* first: win it and you choose your skill yourself.\n",
        "title": "The Spirit Corridor"
      },
      {
        "body": "- `/ttl menu` reopens your current choice.\n- Or right-click the *Voice of the World* in the hall.\n- `/ttl life` shows how your life was judged.\n\nNothing here can hurt you. Take your time.\n",
        "title": "Lost?"
      }
    ],
    "life2": [
      {
        "body": "Open your eyes. You are reborn in the world of Tensura, in *Tempest* in the *Forest of Jura*. *Dwargon* lies to the north.\n\n- Your new race and Unique Skill are yours now. Learn what they can do.\n- Fight, grow stronger and evolve.\n- Death is no longer the end: in Life 2 you come back.\n",
        "title": "Life 2 begins"
      },
      {
        "body": "- `/ttl guide` opens the full guide\n- `/ttl status` tells you which life you are in\n- `/bug <what happened>` sends a report to the developers\n",
        "title": "Need help?"
      }
    ],
    "main": [
      {
        "body": "Every soul here lives *twice*.\n\n- *Life 1:* you are a plain human in the *Mortal Realm*, a world without monsters of legend and without skills. You only live once there.\n- *The Spirit Corridor:* when you die, your soul is judged and you choose what comes next.\n- *Life 2:* you are reborn in the world of Tensura, with a new body and a Unique Skill.\n\nHow you live your first life decides how strong your second one begins.\n",
        "title": "Welcome to Two Lives"
      },
      {
        "body": "You start at *Wayfarer's Rest*. From here the Mortal Realm is yours to explore: it has its own Nether and End.\n\n- There is no second try: Life 1 ends with your first death.\n- When it ends you lose your items, but you keep your XP and advancements.\n- Players can fight each other here: another player can end your only first life, and killing a player darkens your karma.\n- Take your time. A long, full life is worth more than a quick one.\n",
        "title": "Life 1: the Mortal Realm"
      },
      {
        "body": "The world remembers what you do in Life 1. This is your *karma*:\n\n- how long you survive\n- the foes you slay, and above all the great bosses\n- good deeds: trading, defending villages, tending animals\n- mining, smithing, enchanting, brewing and advancements\n\n# Tiers\n*Wanderer*, *Survivor*, *Hero* and *Legend*. A higher tier offers more races at rebirth, and a Hero or Legend chooses their Unique Skill instead of leaving it to fate. A Legend also carries an extra skill.\n\n# The dark path\nKilling villagers, golems, traders or players, or starting raids, stains your soul. A *Fallen* soul is offered dark races.\n\nType `/ttl life` at any time to see your karma and what the next tier needs.\n",
        "title": "Your deeds are judged"
      },
      {
        "body": "When Life 1 ends, the Voice of the World judges your life and your soul arrives in the *Spirit Corridor*.\n\n- *Last Wish:* pick one of ten wishes (Strength, Knowledge, Protection, ...). Your wish decides which Unique Skills can be yours.\n- *Trial of the Soul* (optional): every wish has its own trial. Win and you pick your skill from three; lose and fate picks it.\n- *Rebirth:* the Great Sage's reincarnation ceremony. Choose your new race from your offers (Slime is always one of them).\n- *Unique Skill:* chosen by you or drawn by fate, then you wake up in Life 2.\n\nLost a menu? Type `/ttl menu`, or talk to the *Voice of the World* in the hall.\n",
        "title": "Death and the Spirit Corridor"
      },
      {
        "body": "When Life 1 ends, your body's belongings do not come with you: inventory, armour, ender chest and backpacks are left behind. Your soul keeps:\n\n- your levels, advancements, karma and quest progress\n- your *Soul Gem*: every soul starts with one. It cannot be thrown away in Life 1. In Life 2, right-click it for a short echo of your first life (a few seconds of Regeneration and Resistance, then it rests for a while)\n- a *Remembered Enchantment*: a Hero or Legend whose strongest side was *Craft* is reborn with one enchanted book, the best enchantment they carried, at a lower level\n\nItems from Tensura that you carried into the Mortal Realm are put away safely and come back at rebirth.\n",
        "title": "What your soul keeps"
      },
      {
        "body": "You are reborn on the Tensura continent, in *Tempest* in the *Forest of Jura*. The dwarven kingdom of *Dwargon* lies to the north.\n\n- Your new race and Unique Skill are yours now. Some Unique Skills only a few souls can hold at once.\n- Fight, grow stronger and evolve. Death in Life 2 is not the end: you come back.\n",
        "title": "Life 2: the world of Tensura"
      },
      {
        "body": "- `/ttl guide` opens this guide again\n- `/ttl life` shows your karma and your tier\n- `/ttl status` tells you which life you are in\n- `/ttl menu` reopens your choices in the Spirit Corridor\n- `/bug <what happened>` sends a report to the developers, with everything they need to look into it\n\nFound something odd? Use `/bug` right away, while it is fresh. Good luck, and live well.\n",
        "title": "Useful commands"
      },
      {
        "body": "This is a server for friends. We keep only what we need to run it, and you can ask to see it or have it removed.\n\n# What is stored\n- *Game data:* your Minecraft name and ID, your player file, statistics and your Two Lives progress (life, karma, tier, titles).\n- *Activity log:* a logger records who placed or broke blocks, opened chests, chatted, ran commands and logged in. It lets us undo griefing.\n- *Bug reports:* your text, your position, health, held item, Two Lives state and the latest server log lines. A report can also be filed as an issue on the project's GitHub page, where others can read it.\n- *Discord link:* if you link your account, your Discord ID is stored next to your Minecraft ID and the bot sets your roles. Chat is shared with Discord, and the weekly recap names your character.\n\n# How long\n- Bug reports and the activity log: 180 days at most.\n- Game data and your link: while you play here. Backups roll off after about a month.\n- GitHub issues: until you ask us to remove them.\n\n# Your choices\nAsk Yasuke, in Discord or in game, to show, correct or delete your data, or to unlink your Discord account. Your builds stay with the world.\n",
        "title": "Privacy: what we keep"
      }
    ]
  },
